    {
      "id": "claim_c9cb2a66f89046f3a7176c8802c85329",
      "statement": "The MCP server forwards original error codes and messages instead of replacing them (ADR 0061). parseRouterErrorEnvelope forwards any string code/message from error envelopes (no longer validating against the local BrijioErrorCode union), so relay codes like invalid_message/invalid_json reach the agent. parseErrorPayload preserves stale_context and page_navigated with their structured detail and forwards any other string code (not_supported, cors_blocked, etc.) instead of wrapping as browser_error. BrijioResourceResult and BrijioToolErrorCode error code fields are typed as string to accept arbitrary codes.",
      "evidence": [
