    {
      "id": "claim_bcfc8801ada045d0b173f5e89da9b948",
      "statement": "Action targets use short-lived positional IDs from read_current_page. The content script tracks a pageContextVersion counter incremented on pageshow and returns pageContextId in read_current_page responses. Action envelopes carry optional pageContextId and visibleContextId; a mismatch yields page_navigated (entire snapshot stale, re-read) while validation-field mismatches yield stale_context (re-read and retry). perform_batch can set readAfterActions true to append a fresh page-context read to the batch result. (ADR 0036, ADR 0041)",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0041-reliable-target-identity-and-stale-target-handling.md#L88-L117",
