    {
      "id": "claim_4169168a20d243ef955a420721fdebb6",
      "statement": "The WebSocket relay authenticates each connection by pairing token and scopes all routing by a scopeKey derived from the token hash. Two roles connect: mcp clients (short-lived, one per tool invocation) and extension clients (long-lived). Extensions announce presence (browserInstanceId, label, capabilities) stored in a presence map keyed by scopeKey:browserInstanceId; on socket close the relay drops presence and cleans up pending requests for that socket.",
      "evidence": [
